+        "",
+        f"2. At the source's own 3.32° one-sided width, the corrected-rule correctly paired gap is **{signed_pct(gap_332)}**, with {receipts[('STRICT', '3.32')]['summary']['pairings']['correct']['negative_anchor_count']}/8 negative anchors.",
+        "",
+        f"3. The correctly paired corrected-rule curve is `{'`, `'.join(signed_pct(value) for value in strict_curve)}` and is **{'strictly increasing' if strict_monotone else 'not monotone'}** over the sampled widths. The correctly paired sealed-rule curve is `{'`, `'.join(signed_pct(value) for value in sealed_curve)}` and is **{'strictly increasing' if sealed_monotone else 'not monotone'}**.",
+        "",
+        "No wider width is presented as a remedy for the 1.66° result; any antenna change is a separate design decision outside this diagnostic.",
+        "",
+        "## Correctly paired curve",
+        "",
+        "Pooled efficiency is `sum(bits) / sum(joules)` across the same eight anchors. Negative-anchor counts use each anchor's independently committed 48-boundary efficiency.",
+        "",
+        "| One-sided width | SEALED `J_from_first/U_first` | Negative anchors | STRICT corrected `J_from_first/U_first` | Negative anchors |",
+        "|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|",
+    ]
+    for width in WIDTHS:
+        ss = receipts[("SEALED", width)]["summary"]["pairings"]["correct"]
+        cs = receipts[("STRICT", width)]["summary"]["pairings"]["correct"]
+        lines.append(
+            f"| {width}° | {signed_pct(ss['pooled_relative_ee_gain'])} | {ss['negative_anchor_count']}/8 | {signed_pct(cs['pooled_relative_ee_gain'])} | {cs['negative_anchor_count']}/8 |"
+        )
+
+    lines.extend([
+        "",
+        "## Pooled efficiency and every pairing",
+        "",
+        "`Published` is `J_from_best/U_best`; `correct` is `J_from_first/U_first`. The two cross-pairings are shown because they make the search-order/seed accounting explicit. EE units are Mbit/J.",
+        "",
+        "| Rule | Width | `U_best` EE | `U_first` EE | `J_from_best` EE | `J_from_first` EE | Published gap | Correct gap | `J_best/U_first` | `J_first/U_best` |",
+        "|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|",
+    ])
+    for rule in RULES:
